('shiva-madhya-pradesh-ujjain-mahakaleshwar-temple', 'shiva', 'Mahakaleshwar Temple', NULL, 'Madhya Pradesh', 'Ujjain', 'Shipra River', 'Shiva', 'Shaiva', 'Ujjain offers a powerful jyotirlinga experience with timeless rituals at dawn.', NULL, 'Pre-dawn Bhasma Aarti and Shipra ghats.', NULL, 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Mahakaleshwar%20Temple,%20Ujjain.jpg', 'Wikimedia Commons', 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahakaleshwar_Temple,_Ujjain.jpg', 'Pre-dawn for the signature aarti.', 'Open daily; timings vary by season.', 'Traditional attire recommended.', 'Entry for early aarti often requires prior booking.', '["Jyotirlinga","Bhasma Aarti","Kumbh"]', '["Bhasma aarti","Evening aarti"]', '["Mahashivratri","Kumbh period"]', 'Mahakaleshwar Jyotirlinga is a major Shiva temple in Ujjain and is counted among the twelve jyotirlinga shrines.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Incredible India notes that the Puranas connect Ujjain (Avantika) with Mahakaleshwar, including a Varaha Purana reference that places Mahakaleshwar at the earth\'s central point. It also recounts the Chandrasena-Shrikhar-Dushanan legend that ends with Shiva establishing the jyotirlinga in Ujjain.', NULL, '[{"label":"Incredible India: Mahakaleshwar Temple","url":"https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/madhya-pradesh/ujjain/mahakaleshwar-temple","type":"Government tourism (Purana tradition)"}]', NULL, '[{"label":"Mahakaleshwar Jyotirlinga","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahakaleshwar_Jyotirlinga"}]', 3, 'seed', 'Mahakaleshwar Jyotirlinga', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahakaleshwar_Jyotirlinga', 'verified', 'high', 1.000, '2026-02-19 09:48:12', '2026-02-22 13:34:37', 0),
('shiva-madhya-pradesh-sihoniya-kakanmath-temple-sihoniya-suhoniya', 'shiva', 'Kakanmath Temple (Sihoniya/Suhoniya)', NULL, 'Madhya Pradesh', 'Sihoniya', 'Sihoniya/Suhoniya, Morena district', 'Shiva', 'Shaiva', 'An 11th-century Shiva temple at Sihoniya/Suhoniya, notable for its soaring stone tower and monumental ruined form.', NULL, 'Monumental Shaiva ruin at Sihoniya/Suhoniya.', NULL, 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/0121621_Kakanmath_temple,_Sihoniya_Madhya_Pradesh_026.jpg', 'Wikimedia Commons', 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:0121621_Kakanmath_temple,_Sihoniya_Madhya_Pradesh_026.jpg', 'Winter mornings for clear light.', 'Open daily; timings vary by season.', 'Modest attire recommended.', 'Footwear is not allowed inside temple areas.', '["Heritage","Sihoniya","Shaiva"]', '["Daily puja"]', '["Mahashivratri"]', 'Kakanmath is an 11th-century Shiva temple at Sihoniya, commissioned by the Kachchhapaghata ruler Kirttiraja.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Kakanmath is a ruined 11th-century Shiva temple at Sihoniya, commissioned by the Kachchhapaghata ruler Kirttiraja. The shrine\'s Shaiva dedication anchors its sacred identity in devotion to Shiva rather than to a single Puranic episode.', 'A local folk legend says the temple was named after Queen Kakanavati (Kakanade), though the historicity of this story is considered doubtful. Even so, the name continues to circulate in popular retellings of the site.', '[{"label":"Kakanmath","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kakanmath","type":"Encyclopedia"}]', '[{"label":"Kakanmath","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kakanmath","type":"Encyclopedia (folk legend)"}]', '[{"label":"Kakanmath","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kakanmath"}]', 3, 'seed', 'Kakanmath', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kakanmath', 'verified', 'high', 1.000, '2026-02-19 09:48:12', '2026-02-22 13:34:37', 0),
('shiva-madhya-pradesh-ujjain-kal-bhairav-temple', 'shiva', 'Kal Bhairav Temple', NULL, 'Madhya Pradesh', 'Ujjain', 'Bhairavgarh', 'Shiva (Bhairav)', 'Shaiva', 'A fierce guardian shrine dedicated to Kal Bhairav on the outskirts of Ujjain.', NULL, 'Powerful Bhairav sanctum and devotional offerings.', NULL, 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Kal_Bhairav_temple_Ujjain.jpg', 'Wikimedia Commons', 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kal_Bhairav_temple_Ujjain.jpg', 'Early morning for quieter darshan.', 'Open daily; timings vary by season.', 'Modest attire recommended.', 'Footwear is not allowed inside temple areas.', '["Bhairav","Guardian","Pilgrimage"]', '["Daily puja"]', '["Bhairav Ashtami","Mahashivratri"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Kal Bhairav is revered as the guardian deity of Ujjain, and the temple is linked in tradition to the Avanti Khanda of the Skanda Purana. The shrine\'s identity centers on Bhairav as Shiva\'s fierce protector form.', 'A distinctive local practice is the offering of liquor to the deity, which devotees treat as prasad. This ritual has become one of the most widely retold traditions associated with the temple.', '[{"label":"Kal Bhairav Temple, Ujjain","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kal_Bhairav_Temple,_Ujjain","type":"Encyclopedia"}]', '[{"label":"Kal Bhairav Temple, Ujjain","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kal_Bhairav_Temple,_Ujjain","type":"Encyclopedia (ritual tradition)"}]', '[{"label":"Kal Bhairav Temple, Ujjain","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kal_Bhairav_Temple,_Ujjain"}]', 3, 'seed', 'Kal Bhairav Temple, Ujjain', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kal_Bhairav_Temple,_Ujjain', 'verified', 'high', 1.000, '2026-02-19 09:48:12', '2026-02-22 13:34:37', 0),
('shiva-madhya-pradesh-ujjain-mangalnath-temple', 'shiva', 'Mangalnath Temple', NULL, 'Madhya Pradesh', 'Ujjain', 'Kshipra River', 'Shiva', 'Shaiva', 'Riverside Shiva shrine associated with the planet Mars in Ujjain traditions.', NULL, 'Riverbank darshan and sunrise rituals.', NULL, 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Mangalnath_Ujjain.JPG', 'Wikimedia Commons', 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mangalnath_Ujjain.JPG', 'Sunrise by the river.', 'Open daily; timings vary by season.', 'Modest attire recommended.', 'Footwear is not allowed inside temple areas.', '["Shiva","Kshipra","Mars"]', '["Daily puja","Evening aarti"]', '["Mahashivratri"]', 'Mangalnath is a Shiva temple on the banks of the Shipra in Ujjain and is traditionally associated with Mars (Mangal) worship.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Mangalnath is regarded as the birthplace of Mars (Mangal) according to the Matsya Purana, and the shrine is dedicated to Shiva on the banks of the Shipra. The site was once noted for a clear view of the planet, giving it an astronomical dimension in local sacred geography.', 'Tuesday worship at the Mangal linga draws special crowds, and local practice treats this day as the most auspicious for Mars-related prayers. This weekly ritual rhythm is a key part of the shrine\'s living tradition.', '[{"label":"Mangalnath (Ujjain district)","url":"https://ujjain.nic.in/en/tourist-place/mangalnath/","type":"Government tourism"}]', '[{"label":"Places of Interest (Ujjain district)","url":"https://ujjain.nic.in/en/places-of-interest/","type":"Government tourism"}]', '[{"label":"Mangalnath Temple","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mangalnath"},{"label":"Mangalnath (Ujjain district)","url":"https://ujjain.nic.in/en/tourist-place/mangalnath/"}]', 3, 'seed', 'Mangalnath Temple', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mangalnath', 'verified', 'high', 1.000, '2026-02-19 09:48:12', '2026-02-22 13:34:37', 0),
('shiva-madhya-pradesh-ujjain-siddhavat-temple', 'shiva', 'Siddhavat Temple', NULL, 'Madhya Pradesh', 'Ujjain', 'Kshipra River', 'Shiva', 'Shaiva', 'A sacred riverside temple area associated with ancestral rites and a revered banyan tree.', NULL, 'Rituals by the Kshipra and the ancient banyan.', NULL, 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Ram_Ghat,_Ujjain_01.jpg', 'Wikimedia Commons', 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ram_Ghat,_Ujjain_01.jpg', 'Early morning during river rituals.', 'Open daily; timings vary by season.', 'Modest attire recommended.', 'Footwear is not allowed inside temple areas.', '["Riverbank","Pilgrimage","Rituals"]', '["Daily puja"]', '["Kumbh period","Mahashivratri"]', 'Ujjain district tourism describes Siddhavat as a siddh place on the Shipra and links it to the sacred banyan tradition, comparing it to the Akshay Vat at Prayag.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Ujjain traditions place Siddhavat among the sacred banyans of India and narrate that the vat tree here was planted and worshipped by Parvati. The site is treated as a paapmochan tirtha where rites like shraddha, pind daan, and tarpan are believed to yield special merit.', 'Nath sadhus continue to worship here, and the riverside rituals keep the place active through the year. Siddhavat is also remembered as a key Kshipra bank for ancestral rites during Kumbh cycles.', '[{"label":"Places of Interest (Siddhavat)","url":"https://ujjain.nic.in/en/places-of-interest/","type":"Government tourism"},{"label":"Siddhwat Temple","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siddhwat_Temple","type":"Encyclopedia"}]', '[{"label":"Places of Interest (Siddhavat)","url":"https://ujjain.nic.in/en/places-of-interest/","type":"Government tourism"},{"label":"Siddhwat Temple","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siddhwat_Temple","type":"Encyclopedia"}]', '[{"label":"Places of Interest (Ujjain district)","url":"https://ujjain.nic.in/en/places-of-interest/"}]', 3, 'seed', 'Places of Interest (Ujjain district)', 'https://ujjain.nic.in/en/places-of-interest/', 'verified', 'high', 1.000, '2026-02-19 09:48:12', '2026-02-22 13:34:37', 0),
('shiva-madhya-pradesh-omkareshwar-mamleshwar-amareshwar-temple-south-bank-of-narmada-omkareshwar', 'shiva', 'Mamleshwar (Amareshwar) Temple (South bank of Narmada, Omkareshwar)', NULL, 'Madhya Pradesh', 'Omkareshwar', 'South bank of Narmada, Omkareshwar, Khandwa district', 'Shiva', 'Shaiva', 'The southern-bank shrine paired with Omkareshwar for jyotirlinga darshan.', NULL, 'Riverside darshan and the twin-shrine circuit.', NULL, 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Mamleshwar%20Temple%20Omkareshwar.jpg', 'Wikimedia Commons', 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mamleshwar_Temple_Omkareshwar.jpg', 'Morning darshan by the Narmada bank.', 'Open daily; timings vary by season.', 'Modest traditional attire recommended.', 'Devotees often combine Mamleshwar and Omkareshwar in one visit.', '["Narmada","Omkareshwar","Jyotirlinga Claim"]', '["Abhishekam","Aarti"]', '["Mahashivratri","Shravan month"]', 'The official temple site describes Mamleshwar (Amleshwar) as a revered Shiva temple on the southern bank of the Narmada in Omkareshwar.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The site notes Mamleshwar as the twin jyotirlinga of Omkareshwar and emphasizes darshan at both shrines as part of the pilgrimage.', 'Local practice links Mamleshwar with Narmada parikrama and river aarti traditions around Omkareshwar.', '[{"label":"Shri Mamleshwar Mahadev Mandir","url":"https://shrimamleshwar.org/Default.aspx","type":"Official site"}]', '[{"label":"Shri Mamleshwar Mahadev Mandir (Narmada)","url":"https://www.shrimamleshwar.org/Narmada.aspx","type":"Official site"}]', '[{"label":"Shri Mamleshwar Mahadev Mandir","url":"https://shrimamleshwar.org/Default.aspx"},{"label":"Shri Mamleshwar Mahadev Mandir (Narmada)","url":"https://www.shrimamleshwar.org/Narmada.aspx"}]', 3, 'seed', 'Shri Mamleshwar Mahadev Mandir', 'https://shrimamleshwar.org/Default.aspx', 'verified', 'high', 1.000, '2026-02-19 09:48:12', '2026-02-22 13:34:37', 0),
('shiva-madhya-pradesh-bhojpur-bhojeshwar-bhojpur-mahadev-temple-gauharganj-tehsil', 'shiva', 'Bhojeshwar (Bhojpur) Mahadev Temple (Gauharganj Tehsil)', NULL, 'Madhya Pradesh', 'Bhojpur', 'Bhojpur, Gauharganj tehsil, Raisen district', 'Shiva', 'Shaiva', 'Commissioned in the age of King Bhoja, this monumental yet unfinished temple enshrines one of India\'s largest monolithic Shivalingas and preserves an unusually raw open-circuit architectural energy.', NULL, 'A towering vertical Shiva transmitter centered on a colossal single-stone lingam.', NULL, 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Bhojeshwar%20Temple,%20Bhojpur.jpg', 'Wikimedia Commons', 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhojeshwar_Temple,_Bhojpur.jpg', 'Morning visits for calmer darshan.', 'Open daily; timings vary by season.', 'Modest attire recommended.', 'Heritage site with uneven stone flooring.', '["High Voltage Motherboard","Unfinished Circuit","Monolithic Linga"]', '["Daily puja"]', '["Mahashivratri"]', 'Wikipedia describes Bhojeshwar as an incomplete 11th-century Shiva temple at Bhojpur, associated with Paramara king Bhoja and housing a massive lingam.', 'The sanctum centers on a huge lingam and preserves unfinished architectural elements that reveal the temple\'s construction plan.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The shrine\'s worship centers on Shiva in linga form, with devotion sustained at the historic site.', 'Local tradition links the site to Raja Bhoja\'s temple-building patronage, reinforcing its identity as a Paramara-era Shiva shrine.', '[{"label":"Bhojeshwar Temple","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhojeshwar_Temple","type":"Encyclopedia"}]', '[{"label":"Bhojeshwar Temple","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhojeshwar_Temple","type":"Encyclopedia"}]', '[{"label":"Bhojeshwar Temple","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhojeshwar_Temple"}]', 3, 'seed', 'Bhojeshwar Temple', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhojeshwar_Temple', 'verified', 'high', 1.000, '2026-02-19 09:48:12'