('shiva-madhya-pradesh-mandsaur-pashupatinath-temple', 'shiva', 'Pashupatinath Temple', NULL, 'Madhya Pradesh', 'Mandsaur', 'Mandsaur tehsil, Shivna River', 'Shiva', 'Shaiva', 'A historic Shiva temple on the Shivna River, known for its eight-faced linga.', NULL, 'The rare ashtamukha linga and riverside setting.', NULL, 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Pashupatinath%20Temple%20Mandsaur.jpg', 'Wikimedia Commons', 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pashupatinath_Temple_Mandsaur.jpg', 'Morning darshan by the river.', 'Open daily; timings vary by season.', 'Modest attire recommended.', 'Footwear is not allowed inside temple areas.', '["Ashtamukha","Shivna River","Mandsaur Tehsil"]', '["Daily puja","Abhishekam"]', '["Mahashivratri"]', 'Wikipedia describes the Pashupatinath Temple at Mandsaur as a Shiva temple on the Shivna River, known for its eight-faced linga, with sculpture dated to the 5th-6th century.', 'The temple centers on the rare ashtamukha linga, a distinctive eight-faced icon of Shiva.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The shrine follows the Pashupatinath tradition within Shaivism, honoring Shiva in his Pashupati form.', 'Local reverence emphasizes the ashtamukha linga as the temple\'s central sacred object.', '[{"label":"Pashupatinath Temple, Mandsaur","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pashupatinath_Temple,_Mandsaur","type":"Encyclopedia"}]', '[{"label":"Pashupatinath Temple, Mandsaur","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pashupatinath_Temple,_Mandsaur","type":"Encyclopedia"}]', '[{"label":"Pashupatinath Temple, Mandsaur","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pashupatinath_Temple,_Mandsaur"}]', 3, 'seed', 'Pashupatinath Temple, Mandsaur', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pashupatinath_Temple,_Mandsaur', 'verified', 'high', 1.000, '2026-02-19 09:48:12', '2026-02-22 13:34:37', 0),
('shiva-madhya-pradesh-udaypur-udayeshwara-neelkantheswar-temple-udaypur-ganj-basoda-tehsil', 'shiva', 'Udayeshwara (Neelkantheswar) Temple (Udaypur, Ganj Basoda Tehsil)', NULL, 'Madhya Pradesh', 'Udaypur', 'Udaypur, Ganj Basoda Tehsil, Vidisha district', 'Shiva', 'Shaiva', 'Udayeshwara (Neelkantheswar) Temple at Udaypur is a major Paramara-era Shiva temple in Ganj Basoda Tehsil, built by King Udayaditya between 1059 and 1080 CE.', NULL, 'Premier Bhumija-style Shiva temple with dated Udayaditya-era inscriptions.', NULL, 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Udaipur%20Temple,%20west%20side.jpg', 'Wikimedia Commons', 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Udaipur_Temple,_west_side.jpg', 'Morning visits for a quieter heritage walk.', 'Open daily; timings vary by season.', 'Modest attire recommended.', 'Heritage site; plan route via the Ganj Basoda-Udaypur approach and expect stone pathways.', '["Vidisha","Udaypur","Ganj Basoda Tehsil","Paramara","Bhumija"]', '["Daily puja"]', '["Mahashivratri"]', 'Vidisha district tourism notes the Neelkantheswar (Udayeshwar) temple at Udaypur was built by Paramara king Udayaditya, with inscriptions dating construction to 1059-1080.', 'The temple is recognized as a premier example of Bhumija-style architecture, with a precisely dated medieval stone superstructure.', 'Morning visits are best for heritage viewing and a quieter circuit.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The shrine is dedicated to Shiva as Neelkantheswar, anchoring Shaiva worship in the Udaypur heritage landscape.', 'The Paramara association recorded in inscriptions is a key part of the temple\'s local identity.', '[{"label":"Neelkantheswar Temple (Udaypur)","url":"https://vidisha.nic.in/en/tourist-place/neelkantheswar-temple-udaypur/","type":"Government tourism"}]', '[{"label":"Neelkantheswar Temple (Udaypur)","url":"https://vidisha.nic.in/en/tourist-place/neelkantheswar-temple-udaypur/","type":"Government tourism"}]', '[{"label":"Neelkantheswar Temple (Udaypur)","url":"https://vidisha.nic.in/en/tourist-place/neelkantheswar-temple-udaypur/"}]', 3, 'seed', 'Neelkantheswar Temple (Udaypur)', 'https://vidisha.nic.in/en/tourist-place/neelkantheswar-temple-udaypur/', 'verified', 'high', 1.000, '2026-02-19 09:48:12', '2026-03-17 05:45:00', 0),
('shiva-madhya-pradesh-khajuraho-kandariya-mahadev-temple-khajuraho', 'shiva', 'Kandariya Mahadev Temple (Khajuraho)', NULL, 'Madhya Pradesh', 'Khajuraho', 'Western Group', 'Shiva', 'Shaiva', 'Khajuraho\'s largest and most ornate Shiva temple, famed for sculptural detail.', NULL, 'Rising shikhara towers and intricate Chandela carvings.', NULL, 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Kandariya%20Mahadeva%20Temple.jpg', 'Wikimedia Commons', 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kandariya_Mahadeva_Temple.jpg', 'Morning light for the carvings.', 'Open daily; timings vary by season.', 'Modest attire recommended.', 'Photography is permitted in the outer complex.', '["Khajuraho","Chandela","UNESCO"]', '["Daily puja"]', '["Mahashivratri","Khajuraho Dance Festival"]', 'Wikipedia calls Kandariya Mahadeva the largest and most ornate temple in the Khajuraho group, built around 1025-1050 under the Chandela dynasty.', 'It is a North Indian Nagara-style temple and part of the UNESCO-listed Khajuraho Group of Monuments.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Dedicated to Shiva as Mahadeva, the temple anchors Shaiva worship within the western group of Khajuraho.', 'Khajuraho heritage narratives celebrate Kandariya Mahadeva as the grandest temple of the complex.', '[{"label":"Kandariya Mahadeva Temple","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kandariya_Mahadeva_Temple","type":"Encyclopedia"}]', '[{"label":"Kandariya Mahadeva Temple","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kandariya_Mahadeva_Temple","type":"Encyclopedia"}]', '[{"label":"Kandariya Mahadeva Temple","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kandariya_Mahadeva_Temple"}]', 3, 'seed', 'Kandariya Mahadeva Temple', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kandariya_Mahadeva_Temple', 'verified', 'high', 1.000, '2026-02-19 09:48:12', '2026-02-22 13:34:37', 0),
